export const STAFF_GUIDE_TEXT = "## Get started\nYour admin or supervisor creates your account and gives you a password.\n\n1. Get the Xtend app for your phone from the download page, or open Xtend in Chrome on your phone.\n2. Sign in with the email or phone number your admin registered, and the password you were given. If the page asks you to tick a box first, tick it.\n3. The first time, Xtend asks you to choose your own password. Pick something only you know.\nUsing Chrome instead of the app? Tap the menu, then “Install app” or “Add to Home screen”, so Xtend opens like an app.\n\n## Before your first clock-in\nXtend needs three things switched on before you can clock in. You only do this once per phone.\n\n1. Location: when asked, tap Allow (choose Allow all the time or Always if your phone offers it). In your phone’s settings, set location to High accuracy. In the Xtend app, you also need Battery: Unrestricted (turn off battery saving for Xtend). Xtend will not let you clock in or out until both are set, and it shows you where to change them.\n2. Camera: allow it when asked. Clocking in and out takes a selfie with the camera inside Xtend.\n3. Notifications: tap Turn on notifications on the home screen. You cannot clock in until they are on.\n4. TECNO, Infinix or itel phone? These phones close apps by themselves. Xtend shows Auto-start and lock Xtend: tap Open Auto-start and turn on Xtend, then open your recent apps, pull Xtend down until a lock shows, and tap I did both. You only do this once on each phone.\n\n## Your profile photo\nNew to Xtend? The welcome steps ask for your photo first.\n\n1. The profile menu closes when you tap outside it or press Escape. Go to You and tap Take your photo (or the camera on your picture).\n2. Face the camera in good light and take the photo. Tap it again any time to retake it.\n\n## Clock in\nDo this when you arrive at your store, once a day.\n\nYou can only clock in, or check in at a store, when you are at the store. If you are not, Xtend shows You are off site with the store you need to go to, how far it is and a Directions button that opens the way in Google Maps. Go there, then tap I am at the store. Clocking out works anywhere.\nClock in at your store, never at home or on the way. Clock in by the start time under You, then Your hours: clocking in after it shows as late. Only the office can change your hours.\nMarketers: your day starts at your first store. When you tap Clock in, Xtend asks Pick the store you are starting at and lists your own stores, nearest first, with Here on the one you are in. Pick it, then take the selfie: that clocks you in and checks you in at that store in one go. If you do not clock in at one of your stores, today does not count. See Store visits below.\nHome shows Your next step above the clock controls: it always tells you what to do now, with a button to do it. Use My day below them to see your progress and recent days.\nIf something stops you (location off, a setting Xtend needs, a weak signal indoors), a box pops up with numbered steps to fix it and a Try again button. Do the steps in order.\n\n1. Open Xtend while you are inside your store. If Home cannot load, check your connection and tap Try again.\n2. Below your shift status, tap Clock in with selfie and take a clear photo of your face.\n3. Wait while Xtend checks your location and the photo. When it is done, the home screen shows Clocked in.\n\n## Store visits (marketers)\nMarketers who move between stores check in at each one.\n\n1. Clock in at the start of your day as above. You cannot check in at a store until you have clocked in, and with no signal a check-in or check-out is not recorded: try again when you have signal.\n2. Keep your phone’s location on all day. Without it, Xtend shows Location required and you cannot clock in or out, or check in or out of a store.\n3. Start your day at your first store, never at home. When you open Xtend (or tap Clock in), it asks Pick the store you are starting at. Pick it, and the camera opens: your clock-in selfie also checks you in at that store. Your day only counts once you clock in at a store.\n4. See No stores are allocated to you yet? Message the office the stores you visit, with each store's Google Maps link (open the store in Google Maps, tap Share, copy the link), and clock in once they are added. Do the same for any new store you visit.\n5. At each next store, tap Check in here. If Xtend does not find the store, tap Pick the store myself: it lists only the stores on your list.\n6. While you are checked in, Xtend reminds you every 20 minutes: Still at (the store)? Check out of the store before you leave. If you are still working there, carry on.\n7. When you leave, tap Check out and take a selfie, as when you checked in, before you go to the next store. You can only be checked in at one store at a time. If you forgot to check out of a store, Home shows it with a Check out button: check out, then check in again. Starting your day at one of your stores? Clocking in there checks you in at that store too, so there is no second selfie.\n8. See That store is not on your list? Pick one of your own stores. Working at a new store? Message the office its name and its Google Maps link so they can add it.\n9. If Xtend does not know the place, you must add it before you go on. See Adding a place below.\n\n## Adding a place\nWhen you clock in or check in at a shop or plaza Xtend does not know yet, you must add it before you carry on. You only do this once: after that, Xtend recognises the place for you and everyone else.\n\nYou will see Add this place before you go on at the top of the screen. Until you add it, store visits, stock counts, X Metrics counts and sales, and your daily report wait. You can still clock out at any time.\n\n1. Go outside and stand where you can see the building and its sign. Keep location on.\n2. Type the name exactly as it is written on the sign, for example “Ojota Shopping Plaza” or “Mama Nkechi Provisions”.\n3. Under Photo of the building from outside, with the sign showing, tap Open the camera. Stand still for a few seconds, then take the photo. Take it at the place itself; if Xtend asks you to take it again, stay where you are and retake it.\n4. Under Selfie holding one of our products, tap Open the camera and take a selfie with the product held up next to your face.\n5. Tap Save this place and wait while Xtend checks both photos. When you see Xtend will recognise this place from now on, you are done.\nMarketers: if Xtend does not recognise the store when you check in, tap Pick the store myself and choose it from the list. Stores marked Here are the ones you are standing in.\nBoth photos are taken with the camera in Xtend. You cannot upload a picture from your gallery. The building photo must show a shop or plaza, not a house or the inside of a room. The selfie must show your face and one of our products. If a photo is not accepted, Xtend tells you why: tap the photo again to retake it.\nClocked in somewhere that is not a shop, such as the depot gate? Ask the office: they can let you carry on without adding it.\n\n## Daily report\nIf you see a Report tab at the bottom, file your report each day.\n\n1. Tap Report. First pick which day it is for: Today, Yesterday, another day of the last week, or Another day to choose a date (up to 7 days back). You can write your reports after you clock out: log in again in the evening, or the next morning before you clock in. Then pick what it is for: The whole day, or one of the stores you checked in at that day. You can write one for each store and one for the whole day; each shows Filed · edit once sent.\n2. Fill in how it went, and add a photo if asked.\n3. Have a price list, a display plan, an invoice or a picture for the office? Under Attach documents, tap Choose documents and pick them: PDF, Word, Excel or CSV files, or pictures. Up to 5, each 10 MB or smaller. Each one shows with its name and size; tap the × to take one off.\n4. Tap Submit report. Your documents go with it. You can edit the report, and add or remove documents, for 7 days. Wait for “Updating documents…” to finish before changing another document.\nMarketers: the top of the report shows the store visits it covers: all of that day's for the whole day, or just that one for a store report, with the time in and out and how long you were there. They are added to your report when you save it; there is nothing to type for them.\nNo data? Your report and its documents wait on your phone and send themselves when you get signal. A document you remove with no data shows Removing… until then. A report closes 7 days after the day it is for; after that it cannot be changed.\n\n## Stock count\nWhen a stock count is due, a Count tab appears and the home screen tells you.\n\n1. Tap Count. You see the Xpel stock count sheet: every product, with its barcode. Search by name or barcode to find one quickly.\n2. Tap a product you have and enter how many are in the Back store and on the Shop floor. Xtend adds up the Total. Add the Expiry date and how many were Sold since your last count. Leave out products you do not have.\n3. A product that is not on the sheet goes under Products not on the sheet.\n4. Tap Submit count and take a photo of the shelf showing the products you counted.\nCounts are done when your supervisor asks, and at the end of every month. Prefer paper? Under Count on paper, download the month's sheet for your store, fill it in, and upload it back as the Excel file, a PDF or a photo.\nThe stock count sheet is also on your profile, any day: tap You, then under Stock count sheet tap Download to get this month's sheet for your store as Excel. Fill it in, then tap Upload filled sheet and send the Excel file, a PDF or a photo of it. What you sent this month is listed underneath.\n\n## Clock out\nAt the end of your shift.\n\n1. Marketers: Check out of your last store first.\n2. Tap Clock out with selfie and take the photo.\n3. That is your day done: one clock-in and one clock-out per day. You sign in again the next working day.\nWhen your shift ends, Xtend reminds you to clock out: a message on your phone and a Clock out button at the top of the home screen. If you are still checked in at a store, check out of it first, then clock out.\nXtend also reminds you 5 minutes before your shift starts and 5 minutes before it ends.\nYour working hours are yours, not the store's: you see them on You under Your hours. Clock in by your start time wherever your first store is. If it also says You can clock out from a time, you may clock out any time from then. Only the office can change your hours.\nYou cannot clock out before your clock-out time. If you tap Clock out too early, Xtend says Not time to clock out yet and the time you can clock out from. Marketers: until then, keep checking in and out at your stores. If you must leave early (you are sick, an emergency), call your supervisor: the office can let you clock out now, or clock you out.\n\n## History and your account\nYour own record and settings.\n\nHistory shows your attendance day by day. You shows your account: your store, notifications, Messages, Change your password and Message support. To change your password, type your current password first, then the new one twice. Under Fingerprint and passkeys you can turn on Sign in with fingerprint in the app, so you sign in by touching the sensor instead of typing your password. Your fingerprint stays on your phone. Changing your password turns it off; turn it on again after.\nThe week on the home screen and the calendar in History are coloured:\n\n- A dot: you clocked in that day.\n- Missed (red): a working day you did not clock in.\n- Off (grey): a day off on your schedule.\n- Leave (soft orange): approved leave.\n\n## Days off and leave\nYour supervisor sets which days you work. Ask for leave in the app.\n\n1. Open You, then Ask for leave (it is also on the home screen, under the week).\n2. Pick the type (Annual, Sick, Casual or Other), your first and last day, write the reason, and tap Send request. You can ask for days up to 7 days back.\n3. Your request shows as Pending until your supervisor answers. You get a message when it is Approved or Rejected. You can cancel it while it is still pending.\nOn a day off the home screen says Day off today. Working that day anyway? Clock in as usual.\n\n## Report a problem\nSomething not working, or a complaint? Tell the office from inside Xtend.\n\n1. Go to You, then Message support.\n2. Say what happened, where and when, for example: “my clock-in keeps saying off site at Ikeja City Mall this morning”. One problem per message is easiest to sort out.\n3. The Xtend helper answers simple questions straight away. Anything it cannot sort out goes to the office, and their reply arrives as a notification. Open Message support again to read it or add more.\nUrgent and on shift? Call your supervisor as well.\nTo talk to your supervisor about your work (stock, the store, your shift), open You, then Messages. Write your message and tap Send. Their reply arrives as a notification, and the home screen shows You have a new message until you read it.\n\n## When Xtend stops you\nIf something stops you clocking in, checking in or checking out, a box pops up saying what is wrong, with numbered steps and a button. These are the same steps, so you can read them any time.\n\n### Allow location for Xtend\nXtend cannot clock in or check in without your location, and location is not allowed for Xtend.\nOn Android:\n\n1. Open Settings, then Apps, then Xtend.\n2. Tap Permissions, then Location.\n3. Choose \"Allow all the time\" and turn on \"Use precise location\".\n4. Come back to Xtend and tap Try again.\nOn iPhone:\n\n1. Open Settings on your iPhone.\n2. Scroll down and tap Xtend, then Location.\n3. Choose \"Always\" (or \"While Using the App\") and turn on Precise Location.\n4. Come back to Xtend and tap Try again.\n\n### Turn on Location\nYour phone could not find where you are. Location may be off, or the signal is weak indoors.\nOn Android:\n\n1. Pull down from the top of the screen and turn on Location.\n2. Press and hold Location, and turn on \"Improve accuracy\" (Google Location Accuracy) and Wi-Fi scanning.\n3. Move near the door or a window, or step outside for a moment.\n4. Tap Try again.\nOn iPhone:\n\n1. Open Control Centre or Settings, then Privacy & Security, then Location Services, and turn it on.\n2. Move near the door or a window, or step outside for a moment.\n3. Tap Try again.\n\n### Your location is too rough\nYour phone only knows roughly where you are. Xtend needs it to within 100 m.\nOn Android:\n\n1. Pull down from the top, press and hold Location, and turn on \"Improve accuracy\".\n2. Turn on Wi-Fi (you do not need to connect to a network).\n3. Move near the door or a window, or step outside, and wait a few seconds.\n4. Tap Try again.\nOn iPhone:\n\n1. In Settings, Xtend, Location, turn on Precise Location.\n2. Turn on Wi-Fi (you do not need to connect to a network).\n3. Move near the door or a window, or step outside, and wait a few seconds.\n4. Tap Try again.\n\n### Open Xtend in the app or in Chrome\nThis browser cannot tell Xtend where you are.\n\n1. Open the Xtend app on your phone, or open Xtend in Chrome.\n2. Sign in and try again.\n\n### Finish setting up Xtend to clock in or check in\nSome phone settings Xtend needs are still off, so you cannot clock in or check in yet.\nOn Android:\n\n1. Set Location for Xtend to \"Allow all the time\".\n2. Set Battery for Xtend to \"Unrestricted\" (or turn off battery saving for Xtend).\n3. Come back to Xtend. The card on Home clears by itself when it is done.\nOn iPhone:\n\n1. In Settings, tap Xtend, then Location, and choose \"Always\".\n2. Come back to Xtend. The card on Home clears by itself when it is done.\n\n### Your network is not working\nXtend could not reach the office, so you cannot clock in or check in right now. Your data or signal is off or too weak.\nOn Android:\n\n1. Pull down from the top: check Mobile data is on and Aeroplane mode is off.\n2. Check you have data on your line (airtime or a data plan).\n3. Move near the door or a window, or step outside, where the signal is stronger. Or connect to Wi-Fi.\n4. Tap Try again.\nOn iPhone:\n\n1. Check Mobile Data is on (Settings, Mobile Data) and Aeroplane Mode is off.\n2. Check you have data on your line (airtime or a data plan).\n3. Move near the door or a window, or step outside, where the signal is stronger. Or connect to Wi-Fi.\n4. Tap Try again.\n\n### Weak network: your location is slow\nYour network is off or weak, so your phone is finding where you are slowly and roughly.\n\n1. Turn on Mobile data (and Wi-Fi if there is one nearby; you do not need to connect).\n2. Step outside or near the door, where the signal and the sky are clearer.\n3. Wait a few seconds for the signal bars to come back.\n4. Tap Try again.\n\n### Turn on Xtend notifications\nXtend needs notifications on before you clock in, so the office can reach you during the day.\nOn Android:\n\n1. Open Settings, then Apps, then Xtend, then Notifications.\n2. Turn notifications on.\n3. Come back and tap Try again.\nOn iPhone:\n\n1. Open Settings, then Notifications, then Xtend.\n2. Turn on Allow Notifications.\n3. Come back and tap Try again.\n\n### Take your selfie again\nThe photo could not be used. It must be a live photo of your face, taken in Xtend just now.\n\n1. Face a light (a window or the shop lights), not with the light behind you.\n2. Hold the phone still at arm’s length, your whole face in the picture.\n3. Do not take a photo of a screen or a printed picture.\n4. Tap Try again and take the selfie.\n\n### Your phone’s time is wrong\nThe time on your phone does not match the real time, so Xtend cannot record this.\nOn Android:\n\n1. Open Settings, then Date & time (System).\n2. Turn on Set automatically (and Automatic time zone).\n3. Come back and tap Try again.\nOn iPhone:\n\n1. Open Settings, General, Date & Time.\n2. Turn on Set automatically (and Automatic time zone).\n3. Come back and tap Try again.\n\n### Pick your store first\nYou clock in at the store you are starting your day at. Clocking in also checks you in there.\n\n1. Tap Clock in.\n2. Pick the store you are at from your list.\n3. Take your selfie.\n\n### No stores are allocated to you yet\nYou start your day at one of your stores, so the office must add your stores first.\n\n1. Message the office the list of stores you visit (today and on your usual round).\n2. For each store, open it in Google Maps, tap Share and send the link too, so the office can pin it.\n3. When the office has added them, come back and clock in.\n\n### That store is not on your list\nYou can only start your day at one of the stores allocated to you.\n\n1. Pick one of your own stores instead.\n2. Working at a new store? Message the office its name and its Google Maps link so they can add it.\n\n### Name this place first\nXtend does not know the place you clocked in at. Name it once, then carry on.\n\n1. On Home, tap Name this place.\n2. Take a photo of the store sign outside and a selfie with our product.\n3. Then try again.\n\n### Clock in first\nYou need to be clocked in before you do this.\n\n1. On Home, tap Clock in and take your selfie.\n2. Then try again.\n\n### This is already recorded\nXtend already has this for today. Pull down on Home to see it.\n\n1. Go back to Home and check what it says.\n2. If it looks wrong, message the office.\nStill stuck after the steps? Go to You, then Message support, and say what the box said.\n\n## Questions staff ask\nShort answers to what staff ask most.\n\nQ: Why must I pick a store when I clock in? (marketers)\nA: Your day starts at your first store. Picking it and taking your selfie clocks you in and checks you in there at the same time, so there is only one selfie. If you do not clock in at one of your stores, today does not count.\n\nQ: The store I am at is not on my list\nA: Only the office can add stores to your list. Message them the store's name and its Google Maps link (open the store in Google Maps, tap Share, copy the link). Until it is added, start your day at one of your own stores.\n\nQ: It says no stores are allocated to me\nA: The office has not added your stores yet. Go to You, then Messages, and send the list of stores you visit with each one's Google Maps link. Clock in once they are added.\n\nQ: Can I clock in from home or on the way?\nA: No. Xtend only lets you clock in when you are at your store (marketers: the store you picked to start at). Away from it you see You are off site.\n\nQ: It says “You are off site”\nA: You are not at your store yet. The box names the store you need to be at and how far it is. Tap Directions to see the way in Google Maps, go inside the store, then tap I am at the store and try again. Marketers: if you picked the wrong store, pick the one you are in.\n\nQ: What time should I clock in?\nA: By the start time on You, under Your hours. These are your own hours, whichever store you go to. Clocking in after your start time shows as late. Think your hours are wrong? Message the office: only they can change them.\n\nQ: I keep getting “Still at the store? Check out before you leave”\nA: While you are checked in at a store, Xtend reminds you every 20 minutes so you do not forget to check out. Still working there? Carry on. Leaving? Tap Check out first.\n\nQ: I forgot to check out of a store\nA: Home shows the store with a Check out button. Check out, then check in at the store you are in now. You can only be checked in at one store at a time.\n\nQ: I forgot to clock out\nA: Clock out as soon as you remember. If the day has already ended, message your supervisor so they can sort out your record.\n\nQ: What does “Your next step” on Home mean?\nA: It always tells you what to do now: clock in, check in at a store, check out, write your report or clock out, with a button to do it. Do what it says and your day is in order.\n\nQ: How do I know my clock-in worked?\nA: Home shows Clocked in and the time, and the first ring under My day closes. If you are not sure, pull down on Home to refresh it.\n\nQ: Why does Xtend need a selfie?\nA: It shows it is really you clocking in. Take it in good light with your whole face in the picture. Photos from your gallery cannot be used.\n\nQ: My selfie was not accepted\nA: Face a light (a window or the shop lights), hold the phone still at arm's length and keep your whole face in the picture. Never take a photo of a screen or a printed picture. Then try again.\n\nQ: There is no signal in my store\nA: Step near the door or a window, or outside for a moment, and try again. Reports and stock counts wait on your phone and send themselves when you get signal; a store check-in or check-out needs signal, so try again when you have it.\n\nQ: Home says “No network” or “Your network is weak”\nA: Your data or signal is off or too weak. Turn on Mobile data, check you have data on your line, and move near the door or a window, or step outside. With no network, a clock-in or clock-out is kept on your phone and only counts once it sends; store check-ins and check-outs need network, and your location is slower to find. When it says Your network is back, anything waiting sends by itself.\n\nQ: I got a new phone\nA: Install Xtend from the download page, sign in, and allow Location, Camera and Notifications again, as in Before your first clock-in. Your record stays with your account, not the phone.\n\nQ: How do I change my profile photo?\nA: Go to You and tap your picture (or Take your photo), then take a new one.\n\nQ: I missed my daily report yesterday\nA: Open Report and pick Yesterday (or another day, up to 7 days back). After 7 days a report can no longer be written or changed.\n\nQ: I am sick or need a day off\nA: Go to You, then Ask for leave, pick Sick or another type, the days and the reason. Call your supervisor too if it is the same day.\n\nQ: Who answers when I message support?\nA: The Xtend helper answers simple questions straight away. Anything it cannot sort out goes to the office, and you get a notification when they reply.\n\nQ: Where is this guide in the app?\nA: Go to You, then How to use Xtend. Every pop-up also has a link: Not sure? Read the staff guide.\n\n## Common problems\n\nQ: It says my location is blocked\nA: Open your phone’s Settings, then Apps (or Privacy on iPhone), then Xtend or Chrome, and allow Location. Set location to High accuracy, then go back to Xtend.\n\nQ: My location is not accurate enough\nA: Turn location on with High accuracy, step outside or near a window for a moment, then tap Try again.\n\nQ: It says I am off site, but I am in my store\nA: Try again near the entrance or a window, so your phone finds you. If it keeps happening, call your supervisor (they can clock you in) and tell support through Message support so your store’s location can be checked.\n\nQ: Notifications are blocked\nA: In the app: open your phone’s Settings, then Apps (or Notifications on iPhone), then Xtend, and turn Notifications on. In Chrome: tap the lock icon next to the web address, choose Notifications and set it to Allow. On iPhone without the app, add Xtend to your home screen first (Share, then “Add to Home Screen”) and open it from there.\n\nQ: The camera does not open\nA: Allow the camera for Xtend in your phone’s settings, close other apps using the camera, and try again.\n\nQ: A banner says something is waiting to send\nA: It sends by itself when you have signal. Keep working, and do not sign out until it has gone.\n\nQ: The phone says “App not installed” or “package appears to be invalid”\nA: Uninstall any old Xtend first (hold its icon, then Uninstall), then open the file from the download page again and tap Install.\n\nQ: Xtend says “No connection”\nA: Check your data or Wi-Fi, then tap Try again.\n\nQ: The app would not clock me in or out\nA: Call your supervisor. When they confirm you are at the store, they can clock you in or out for you, and you get a notification. If they ask you to clock in or out again, Home shows it: just do it again as usual.\n\nQ: I forgot my password\nA: Ask your supervisor or admin to reset it. You will choose a new one when you sign in.\n\nQ: It says “Turn your location back on”\nA: Your location was switched off. Tap the message (or open your phone's settings) and turn Location on. Keep it on from when you clock in until you clock out.\n\nQ: It says “Install the new Xtend app”\nA: A new Xtend app came out and you were reminded three times. Tap Get the new app and install it; Xtend opens again straight away. Your account and anything waiting to send are kept. Update when the first reminder comes, so this never stops your work.\n\nQ: It says “Your account is paused”\nA: Contact your supervisor or admin. They will tell you what to do next.\n\nQ: It says signing in is paused\nA: After 5 wrong passwords in a row, Xtend pauses signing in on that phone for 15 minutes to keep your account safe. Wait, then try again with the right password, or ask your supervisor to unlock it sooner."
